# Onwarda Git identity

Use the repository-configured identity `Luqmeh <93534158+Luqmeh@users.noreply.github.com>`.

Before creating a commit, verify the effective author and committer with `git var GIT_AUTHOR_IDENT` and `git var GIT_COMMITTER_IDENT`. Both must use that email.

Do not intentionally author commits as `metal` or any other unrecognized identity.

Do not override the configured identity with `git -c user.name`, `git -c user.email`, `--author`, or `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*` environment variables.

After each new commit, verify its author with `git show -s --format='%an <%ae>' HEAD` before pushing.

Do not bypass a Git push guard with `--no-verify`.

In a fresh checkout, if `git config --get core.hooksPath` is empty, set it to `.githooks` so `.githooks/pre-push` rejects outgoing commits whose author email is not `93534158+Luqmeh@users.noreply.github.com`.

Preserve unrelated local changes. Do not rewrite published history without explicit approval.
